{"kind": "ask", "id": "20261022T173440Z-e6c74d", "time": "2026-10-22T17:34:40+00:00", "assembly": "toy-ca/demo", "question": "How likely is each origin to be cut off from n1 and n2?", "llm": {"provider": "anthropic", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, "answer": "What does 'cut off from n1 and n2' mean for each origin? The model's built-in system event (SystemState) is defined by the 'reach-key-destination' requirement, which allows 0.5 h of added travel time. It is not a pure connectivity test. Which requirement should I use? I'll use the default M7.8 demo San Andreas scenario unless you name another hazard.\n- Built-in system event: P(SystemState::origin == 0 | H): the origin fails the model's reach-key-destination requirement (added travel time over 0.5 h), as currently defined.\n- Cut off from both: P(no open path from the origin to n1 AND no open path to n2 | H): the origin can reach neither destination.\n- Cut off from either: P(no open path to n1 OR no open path to n2 | H): the origin loses access to at least one of the two destinations.", "clarification": {"question": "What does 'cut off from n1 and n2' mean for each origin? The model's built-in system event (SystemState) is defined by the 'reach-key-destination' requirement, which allows 0.5 h of added travel time. It is not a pure connectivity test. Which requirement should I use? I'll use the default M7.8 demo San Andreas scenario unless you name another hazard.", "missing": ["system_requirement"], "choices": [{"label": "Built-in system event", "definition": "P(SystemState::origin == 0 | H): the origin fails the model's reach-key-destination requirement (added travel time over 0.5 h), as currently defined."}, {"label": "Cut off from both", "definition": "P(no open path from the origin to n1 AND no open path to n2 | H): the origin can reach neither destination."}, {"label": "Cut off from either", "definition": "P(no open path to n1 OR no open path to n2 | H): the origin loses access to at least one of the two destinations."}]}, "history": [], "translations": []}
