{"kind": "ask", "id": "20261022T173509Z-be0cb5", "time": "2026-10-22T17:35:09+00:00", "assembly": "toy-ca/demo", "question": "Built-in system event: P(SystemState::origin == 0 | H): the origin fails the model's reach-key-destination requirement (added travel time over 0.5 h), as currently defined.", "llm": {"provider": "anthropic", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, "answer": "I ran one query: the probability that each origin fails its built-in system event (SystemState == 0). This used the default M7.8 demo San Andreas scenario with 100,000 Monte Carlo samples.\n\n| Origin | P(fails requirement) | 95% interval |\n|---|---|---|\n| n4 | 0.14 | 0.139–0.143 |\n| n6 | 0.11 | 0.108–0.112 |\n| n5 | 0.091 | 0.089–0.093 |\n| n8 | 0.022 | 0.021–0.022 |\n| n3 | 0.011 | 0.010–0.012 |\n| n7 | 0.0028 | 0.0025–0.0031 |\n\n**n4 is the most exposed (about 1 in 7)**, followed by n6 and n5. n7 is the least exposed.\n\nThings to keep in mind:\n- **What the event measures:** each number is the chance the origin breaks the model's \"reach-key-destination\" rule (more than 0.5 h of added travel time). It is not a pure test of whether n1 and n2 can still be reached at all.\n- **Results from different origins can't be combined:** the model treats each bridge's shaking as independent of its neighbours, so it probably understates the chance of several origins failing together. The numbers above are fine one origin at a time.\n- **Demo-only model:** the ground-motion model is a stand-in for illustration, not a real hazard assessment.", "clarification": null, "history": [{"role": "user", "content": "How likely is each origin to be cut off from n1 and n2?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "What does 'cut off from n1 and n2' mean for each origin? The model's built-in system event (SystemState) is defined by the 'reach-key-destination' requirement, which allows 0.5 h of added travel time. It is not a pure connectivity test. Which requirement should I use? I'll use the default M7.8 demo San Andreas scenario unless you name another hazard.\n- Built-in system event: P(SystemState::origin == 0 | H): the origin fails the model's reach-key-destination requirement (added travel time over 0.5 h), as currently defined.\n- Cut off from both: P(no open path from the origin to n1 AND no open path to n2 | H): the origin can reach neither destination.\n- Cut off from either: P(no open path to n1 OR no open path to n2 | H): the origin loses access to at least one of the two destinations."}], "translations": [{"statement": "P(SystemState[*] = 0)   [BN toy-ca/demo]", "query": {"assembly": "toy-ca/demo", "events": [{"node": "SystemState::*", "op": "==", "value": 0}], "samples": 100000}, "record": "20261022T173502Z-7deb29", "refused": null}]}
