{"kind": "ask", "id": "20261022T173601Z-9f0c71", "time": "2026-10-22T17:36:01+00:00", "assembly": "toy-ca/demo", "question": "What would retrofitting b2 to HWB11 do to n4's chance of being cut off?", "llm": {"provider": "anthropic", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, "answer": "Retrofitting b2 to HWB11 would cut n4's chance of failing its requirement **by about 1.4 percentage points, from 0.14 to 0.13.** It helps a little, but n4 still fails in about 1 run in 8.\n\nI ran the same query twice under the default M7.8 demo scenario, with 100,000 samples each: the probability that n4 fails its built-in system event (SystemState::n4 = 0), first as the model stands and then with b2 changed to HWB11.\n\n| Case | P(n4 fails) | 95% interval |\n|---|---|---|\n| As the model stands | 0.14 | 0.139–0.143 |\n| b2 retrofitted to HWB11 | 0.13 | 0.125–0.129 |\n\n- **Size of the change:** a separate comparison tool put the drop at 1.4 percentage points. That tool gives no confidence interval for the difference. However, the two intervals above don't overlap, so the drop is unlikely to be just sampling noise.\n- **What the event measures:** \"cut off\" here means the model's built-in rule for n4, which is more than 0.5 h of added travel time to its key destination. It is not a pure test of whether n4 can still reach anything.\n- **Demo-only model:** the ground-motion model is a stand-in for illustration, not a real hazard assessment.", "clarification": null, "history": [{"role": "user", "content": "How likely is each origin to be cut off from n1 and n2?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "What does 'cut off from n1 and n2' mean for each origin? The model's built-in system event (SystemState) is defined by the 'reach-key-destination' requirement, which allows 0.5 h of added travel time. It is not a pure connectivity test. Which requirement should I use? I'll use the default M7.8 demo San Andreas scenario unless you name another hazard.\n- Built-in system event: P(SystemState::origin == 0 | H): the origin fails the model's reach-key-destination requirement (added travel time over 0.5 h), as currently defined.\n- Cut off from both: P(no open path from the origin to n1 AND no open path to n2 | H): the origin can reach neither destination.\n- Cut off from either: P(no open path to n1 OR no open path to n2 | H): the origin loses access to at least one of the two destinations."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Built-in system event: P(SystemState::origin == 0 | H): the origin fails the model's reach-key-destination requirement (added travel time over 0.5 h), as currently defined."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I ran one query: the probability that each origin fails its built-in system event (SystemState == 0). This used the default M7.8 demo San Andreas scenario with 100,000 Monte Carlo samples.\n\n| Origin | P(fails requirement) | 95% interval |\n|---|---|---|\n| n4 | 0.14 | 0.139–0.143 |\n| n6 | 0.11 | 0.108–0.112 |\n| n5 | 0.091 | 0.089–0.093 |\n| n8 | 0.022 | 0.021–0.022 |\n| n3 | 0.011 | 0.010–0.012 |\n| n7 | 0.0028 | 0.0025–0.0031 |\n\n**n4 is the most exposed (about 1 in 7)**, followed by n6 and n5. n7 is the least exposed.\n\nThings to keep in mind:\n- **What the event measures:** each number is the chance the origin breaks the model's \"reach-key-destination\" rule (more than 0.5 h of added travel time). It is not a pure test of whether n1 and n2 can still be reached at all.\n- **Results from different origins can't be combined:** the model treats each bridge's shaking as independent of its neighbours, so it probably understates the chance of several origins failing together. The numbers above are fine one origin at a time.\n- **Demo-only model:** the ground-motion model is a stand-in for illustration, not a real hazard assessment."}], "translations": [{"statement": "P(SystemState[n4] = 0)   [BN toy-ca/demo]", "query": {"assembly": "toy-ca/demo", "events": [{"node": "SystemState::n4", "op": "==", "value": 0}], "samples": 100000}, "record": "20261022T173537Z-d09e11", "refused": null}, {"statement": "P(SystemState[n4] = 0) | do(b2.hazus_class = HWB11)   [BN toy-ca/demo]", "query": {"assembly": "toy-ca/demo", "events": [{"node": "SystemState::n4", "op": "==", "value": 0}], "rows": {"b2": {"hazus_class": "HWB11"}}, "samples": 100000}, "record": "20261022T173547Z-3d7b8b", "refused": null}, {"statement": "P(SystemState[n4] = 0)   [BN toy-ca/demo]", "query": {"assembly": "toy-ca/demo", "events": [{"node": "SystemState::n4", "op": "==", "value": 0}], "samples": 100000}, "record": "20261022T173553Z-ac2e92", "refused": null}, {"statement": "P(SystemState[n4] = 0) | do(b2.hazus_class = HWB11)   [BN toy-ca/demo]", "query": {"assembly": "toy-ca/demo", "events": [{"node": "SystemState::n4", "op": "==", "value": 0}], "rows": {"b2": {"hazus_class": "HWB11"}}, "samples": 100000}, "record": "20261022T173554Z-b6b4c6", "refused": null}]}
